    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "93873e47b8cb9bb94a2435617185f1af158a908803346e8cecdadac41f4d9636",
      "text": "Head to the airport early in the morning for your flight to Pereira. Once you arrive, you’ll begin exploring Colombia’s coffee region.\n\nThe main visit of the day is to El Ocaso Coffee Farm. It sits about 1,500 m above sea level, on volcanic soil in the Central Cordillera of the Colombian Andes.\n\nA local specialist leads the tour. You’ll learn how coffee plants are planted, how the cherries are picked selectively by hand and how to tell when they’re ripe. You’ll then see how the harvest is processed.\n\nThe beans are roasted over a wood fire in the kitchen of a traditional country house. Along the way, you’ll make several stops overlooking the hills and plantations, where you can try freshly brewed coffee.\n\nYou’ll also see how the beans are dried and how the processing equipment works. The visit finishes with coffee lemonade at the farm, followed by a transfer to your hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9larkh-8ge0qr1dl",
        "model": "GPT-6.1-sol"
      }
    },
